#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0305-A expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "PLAN-scalar-date-extremes: EX has NO POOLID column; POOLDEF assigns 001 to P1 and carries a second row for 001 with a BLANK POOLID; own 001 2020-01-05, 002 2020-01-01; RFXSTDTC = each own earliest -> silent. Pin of the pool binding's filter=(not empty(POOLID)): without it all EX rows are one block keyed blank, which the blank-POOLID POOLDEF row takes as 001's pool part (2020-01-01) -> 001 reported. The 7 filter sabotage reds this scenario. ⚑ PLAN-join-key-one-side-absent-drop QK17 (owner 2026-10-11): split by the pool gate — POOLDEF defines pools but EX has no POOLID: the pool part cannot be read, so both CDISC-SEND-0305 and CDISC-SEND-0305-A SKIP (was noViolation)"
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFXSTDTC type=Char label="Date/Time of First Study Treatment"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-01-05
S1 | DM | 002 | 2020-01-01
---
dataset EX class=INTERVENTIONS label="Exposure"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col EXSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col EXTRT   type=Char label="Name of Treatment"
col EXSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Treatment"
---
S1 | EX | 001 | 1 | DRUG A | 2020-01-05
S1 | EX | 002 | 2 | DRUG A | 2020-01-01
---
dataset POOLDEF label="Pool Definition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | P1 | 001
S1 |  | 001
---
